#: ../../../reference/interfaces/index.md:0
msgid ""
"Browse every snap interface and learn how snap users and developers can "
"connect, manage, and use system resources securely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/index.md:8
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/index.md:10
msgid ""
"{ref}`Interfaces <explanation-interfaces-all-about-interfaces>` enable "
"resources from one snap to be shared with another and with the system. The "
"table below lists currently supported interfaces, with links to further "
"details for each interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/index.md:12
msgid "The following column names are used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/index.md:14
msgid "**Interface** is the syntactical interface name, as used by snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/index.md:16
msgid ""
"**Description** is a brief overview of what the interface permits. Select "
"the interface name to open the interface-specific page for a more detailed "
"description on each interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/index.md:18
msgid ""
"**Categories** are used to split interfaces into broad types, and also to "
"indicate what kind of access they permit. Video, graphics and audio are "
"typical desktop requirements, for example, while VM, Container, Kernel and "
"Developer imply more specific roles. The Ubuntu Core category is used to "
"denote when an interface is intended for {ref}`Ubuntu Core <ref-"
"glossary_ubuntu-core>`, and _Super privileged_ is used when an interface "
"requires extra security scrutiny. See {ref}`Super-privileged interfaces "
"<reference-operations-interfaces-super-privileged-interfaces>` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/index.md:20
msgid ""
"**Auto-connect** indicates that the interface will be connected by default "
"when the snap is first installed, requiring no further user action. If `Auto-"
"connect=no`, an interface can still be automatically connected if the snap "
"developer has requested, and been granted, explicit permission. See {ref}"
"`Interface connection mechanism <explanation-interfaces-all-about-"
"interfaces>` for details."
msgstr ""

